---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import journeyMap1 from '../../assets/images/journey-map-1.png';
import journeyMap2 from '../../assets/images/journey-map-2.png';
import raaJourney from '../../assets/images/raa-journey.png';
import raaPersona from '../../assets/images/raa-persona.png';
---
<Layout title="Journey Mapping | Andrew Smith" description="Journey maps that connect real metrics, research, and pain points — making member experience visible and actionable.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="case-page">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="case-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><a class="breadcrumb-link" href="/portfolio/work">Work</a><span class="breadcrumb-separator">/</span><span>Journey Mapping</span></p>
        <h1 class="display-title">Making member experience visible and actionable.</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">A journey map is only useful if it stays connected to real data and real decisions. The examples below show two different approaches — a live, metrics-connected journey explorer and a research-grounded static map — both built to be referenced, not filed away.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="meta-strip">
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Organisation</p><p class="meta-value">RAA</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Role</p><p class="meta-value">Senior UX Design Lead</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Scope</p><p class="meta-value">Insurance, travel, identity</p></div>
      </section>
      <section class="lead-image-section">
        <Image class="lead-image" src={journeyMap1} alt="QTB Journey Explorer showing phases, win rates, drop-offs, emotion curve, and prioritised solutions" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="summary-section">
        <p class="section-kicker">QTB Journey Explorer</p>
        <h2>A journey map connected to live metrics and a prioritised solution backlog.</h2>
        <div class="summary-main">
          <p>The Quote to Buy journey explorer connects real analytics data to each stage of the member journey — win rates, drop-offs, failure rates, and emotion scores — alongside a prioritised backlog of solutions rated by member value and business value. A team using this map can point to exactly where the experience breaks down and what to do about it.</p>
          <p>This is what journey management looks like when it works: not a slide in a presentation, but a living reference that shapes what gets built next.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={journeyMap2} alt="QTB Journey Explorer with solution detail panel open showing priority, effort, member value, and business value ratings" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">Research-Grounded Maps</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>Before digital journey management platforms, maps were built from research synthesis — interviews, usability sessions, analytics, and team knowledge combined into a shared artefact. The RAA Travel map below shows the full member journey from Instagram inspiration through to booking confirmation, with moods, touchpoints, pain points, and opportunities mapped at each stage.</p>
          <p>The persona that informed this map — Ali, a young professional RAA member — grounds every design decision in a real person's motivations, not a demographic average.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={raaJourney} alt="RAA Travel journey map showing stages from research through booking, with moods, touchpoints, pain points, and opportunities" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={raaPersona} alt="User persona for RAA Travel — Ali, 32, young professional RAA member" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
.case-page{position:relative;width:min(calc(100% - 3rem),78rem);margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 0 5rem}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}
.breadcrumb-link{font-weight:600}.breadcrumb-separator{color:var(--muted-foreground)}
h1,h2{margin:0;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.05em;color:var(--foreground)}
.display-title{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.06;margin:1rem 0 0;max-width:28ch}
.hero-text,.story-block p,.summary-main p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem}
.case-hero{padding:5rem 0 2rem}
.meta-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem;padding:1.5rem 0 .5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.meta-label{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0}
.meta-value{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700}
.lead-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem}
.lead-image,.supporting-image{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1.5rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-large)}
.supporting-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section{padding:0 0 3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section h2{margin-top:.75rem;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2.2rem);max-width:32ch}
.summary-main{margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:44rem}
.section-kicker{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 .5rem}
.editorial-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:14rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.story-block{max-width:44rem}
</style>
